sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Newt kidney tubules normally made of 8 to 10 cells in cross-section are built from fewer cells when cell size is experimentally enlarged, and from a single cell wrapping around itself when cells are made very large, showing that different molecular mechanisms (cell-cell interactions vs cytoskeletal deformation) can be deployed to reach the same anatomical outcome.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Newt kidney tubules keep correct lumen size when cell size changes";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: An Experimentally-Grounded Framework for Understanding Diverse Bodies and Minds”, Frontiers in systems neuroscience (2022), doi:10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201; section “Somatic Cognition: An Example of Unconventional Agency in Detail › Multi-Scale Competency of Growth and Form”. Scope: Polyploid newt larvae (Fankhauser's experiments)"
}
